---

<AudienceLanding {...page}>
  <section slot="after-solution" class="section corporate-choice-panel mission-cohort-offer">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading audience-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">What the sponsor receives</p><h2>One clear report with useful evidence underneath.</h2></div>
        <p>We agree the evidence framework before delivery begins, then show both the shared picture and the differences that matter locally.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mission-cohort-grid">
        <ol class="mission-cohort-steps">
          <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Reach</h3><p>Who accessed support and whether priority groups were reached.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Engagement</h3><p>Plans, repeat use, actions and trusted resources accessed.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Service movement</h3><p>Referrals, warm handovers and meaningful journey milestones.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Outcomes and learning</h3><p>Confidence, stability, wellbeing, progression, operational value and the next decision.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <aside class="sponsor-report-card">
          <span>Start focused</span><h3>Design a two to five member mission cohort.</h3>
          <ul><li><strong>One mission</strong><small>A clear population, place or outcome</small></li><li><strong>Trusted members</strong><small>Relevant social enterprises with real expertise</small></li><li><strong>Shared infrastructure</strong><small>AI coaches, onboarding and continued support</small></li><li><strong>Proportionate evidence</strong><small>Useful measures without burdensome reporting</small></li></ul>
          <a href="#book-a-call">Discuss a cohort <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</AudienceLanding>
